.TH dbranch 1 2026-09-25 "sandogasa 0.25.1" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
dbranch \- Propagate a Debian package across its Ubuntu PPA and Debian branches
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdbranch\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Propagate a Debian package across its Ubuntu PPA and Debian branches
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS dbranch clone
\fBdbranch clone\fR [\fB\-\-upstream\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-debian\-branch\fR] [\fB\-\-upstream\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-from\-upstream\-packaging\fR] [\fB\-\-fresh\fR] [\fB\-\-salsa\fR] [\fB\-\-mr\fR] [\fB\-\-mrconfig\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIURL\fR> [\fIDIR\fR] 
.PP
Clone upstream\*(Aqs git to package it straight from its tags (gbp\*(Aqs
"upstream uses git, no tarballs" flow): clone with upstream as
remote `upstream`, start the Debian branch at the newest release tag,
and commit a debian/gbp.conf naming the tag style (upstream\-tag) with
pristine\-tar enabled. When upstream itself carries a debian/* branch,
offers to start from it instead (its packaging commits stay in the
history, so diverging is ordinary commits), merging the tag in.
\-\-salsa NAMESPACE also creates the packaging project on salsa and adds
it as origin (the first push is `update \-\-stage push`, which adds the
CI file); \-\-mr registers the clone with myrepos.
Later releases are then merged in by `update`,
which detects this layout, and the source stage generates the orig
tarball from the tag with `gbp export\-orig`. Writing the rest of
debian/ is left to you.
.TP
\fB\-\-upstream\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
Upstream release to start from (default: the newest tag)
.TP
\fB\-\-debian\-branch\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR [default: debian/latest]
Debian packaging branch to create
.TP
\fB\-\-upstream\-remote\fR \fI<NAME>\fR [default: upstream]
Name for the remote holding upstream\*(Aqs git
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-upstream\-packaging\fR
Start from upstream\*(Aqs own debian/* branch without asking
.TP
\fB\-\-fresh\fR
Ignore any debian/* branch upstream carries; start at the tag
.TP
\fB\-\-salsa\fR \fI<NAMESPACE>\fR
Create the packaging project on salsa.debian.org in this namespace and add it as origin (pushing is `update`\*(Aqs job)
.TP
\fB\-\-mr\fR
Register the clone with myrepos (mr config)
.TP
\fB\-\-mrconfig\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
mrconfig to register in (default: ~/.mrconfig)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the commands without running anything (a tutorial)
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Run, but narrate each step + command first (follow along)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress tool output, showing it only when a step fails
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIURL\fR>
Upstream git URL
.TP
[\fIDIR\fR]
Directory to clone into (default: the repository\*(Aqs name)
.SS dbranch fixup
\fBdbranch fixup\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIBRANCH\fR] 
.PP
Fix up gbp.conf / salsa\-ci.yml on existing PPA branch(es)
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR [default: .]
Run in this package working directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the commands without running anything (a tutorial)
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Run, but narrate each step + command first (follow along)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress tool output, showing it only when a step fails
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIBRANCH\fR]
Branch(es) to fix up (default: the current branch)
.SS dbranch rebuild
\fBdbranch rebuild\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-stage\fR] [\fB\-\-source\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-nowait\fR] [\fB\-\-refresh\-chroot\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-refresh\-chroot\fR] [\fB\-\-urgency\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-eol\fR] [\fB\-\-ppa\fR] [\fB\-\-upload\-target\fR] [\fB\-\-debusine\fR] [\fB\-\-debusine\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIBRANCH\fR] 
.PP
Rebuild a Debian package across its Ubuntu/PPA branches
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR [default: .]
Run in this package working directory
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIBRANCH\fR]
PPA branch(es) to rebuild, repeatable or comma\-
separated. Run from the Debian branch (the merge
source). A branch that doesn\*(Aqt exist is created from
it (codename = the name\*(Aqs basename). With none given,
all local branches except the current one and gbp\*(Aqs
upstream / pristine\-tar branches are rebuilt.
.SH STAGES
.TP
\fB\-\-stage\fR \fI<STAGE>\fR
Stages to run, repeatable or comma\-separated:
  merge   merge the Debian branch + write the rebuild
          changelog entry
  source  debuild \-S the source package (\-sa unless
          uploading to the Debian archive)
  build   pbuilder\-dist scratch build of the .dsc
  lint    lintian on the built source package (warns,
          does not fail the run)
  push    git push the branch, then watch its CI
          pipeline via glab (see \-\-nowait)
  upload  dput the built package (needs \-\-ppa or
          \-\-upload\-target)
  tag     dh clean + gbp tag the release
  all     merge + source + build + lint + push
          (upload and tag are opt\-in)
Defaults to `merge` (the others are opt\-in for now).
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fI<BRANCH>\fR
Merge source branch (default: the checked\-out branch)
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Git remote to push to and configure CI on (default: the branch\*(Aqs own, else the only one; asks when several could)
.TP
\fB\-\-nowait\fR
In the push stage, push but don\*(Aqt wait for / watch CI
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-chroot\fR
Build stage: force\-refresh the pbuilder chroot first
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-refresh\-chroot\fR
Build stage: never auto\-refresh the pbuilder chroot
.TP
\fB\-\-urgency\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR [default: medium]
Changelog urgency (default medium; e.g. high for security)
.SH "BULK (NO BRANCHES GIVEN)"
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Bulk run: skip the branch\-set confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-eol\fR
Bulk run: include EOL Ubuntu releases (default skips them)
.SH UPLOAD
.TP
\fB\-\-ppa\fR \fI<PPA>\fR
Upload stage: target PPA (e.g. `user/name`; `ppa:` optional)
.TP
\fB\-\-upload\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR
Upload stage: dput target host (e.g. `mentors`, `ftp\-master`)
.TP
\fB\-\-debusine\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Upload stage: publish to a Debusine personal repository instead of a
dput archive. NAME is the repository owner (the r\-NAME\-* workspace
prefix on debusine.debian.net); dbranch uploads with
  dput \-O debusine_workspace=r\-NAME\-<srcpkg>
       \-O debusine_workflow=publish\-to\-<suite>\-<srcpkg>
(\-\-debusine\-project replaces <srcpkg> for shared workspaces)
where <suite> is the target\*(Aqs base release (a trixie backport
publishes to trixie). Debian targets only. Needs debusine\-client and
a `debusine setup` token.
See wiki.debian.org/DebusineDebianNet#Repositories.
.TP
\fB\-\-debusine\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
Upload stage: the Debusine project name — the part after the owner
in the r\-NAME\-PROJECT workspace and publish\-to\-<suite>\-PROJECT
workflow. Defaults to the source package name, which fits a repo
shipping one package; a shared workspace hosting several packages
names its project here. Requires \-\-debusine.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the commands without running anything (a tutorial)
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Run, but narrate each step + command first (follow along)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress tool output, showing it only when a step fails
.SS dbranch update
\fBdbranch update\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-stage\fR] [\fB\-\-build\-suite\fR] [\fB\-\-upstream\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-upstream\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-nowait\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-refresh\-chroot\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-refresh\-chroot\fR] [\fB\-\-urgency\fR] [\fB\-\-upload\-target\fR] [\fB\-\-debusine\fR] [\fB\-\-debusine\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIBRANCH\fR] 
.PP
Update the Debian branch to a new upstream release
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR [default: .]
Run in this package working directory
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to prompts (e.g. create a missing Debusine workspace) instead of asking
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIBRANCH\fR]
Debian branch to update (defaults to the current branch)
.SH STAGES
.TP
\fB\-\-stage\fR \fI<STAGE>\fR
Stages to run, repeatable or comma\-separated:
  import  gbp import\-orig \-\-uscan + gbp dch \-c \-R; or,
          when packaging from upstream\*(Aqs git (see
          `clone`), merge its release tag instead
  source  debuild \-S the source package (\-si for the
          Debian archive, \-sa for anywhere else)
  build   pbuilder\-dist scratch build of the .dsc
  lint    lintian on the built source package
  push    git push the branch, then watch its CI
  upload  dput the built package
  tag     dh clean + gbp tag the release
  all     import + source + build + lint + push
Defaults to `import`.
.TP
\fB\-\-build\-suite\fR \fI<SUITE>\fR [default: testing]
Debian suite to build against (e.g. `unstable`)
.TP
\fB\-\-upstream\-remote\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Remote holding upstream\*(Aqs git, to merge releases from (default: one named `upstream`, if present)
.TP
\fB\-\-upstream\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
Upstream release to merge in (default: the newest tag)
.TP
\fB\-\-nowait\fR
In the push stage, push but don\*(Aqt wait for / watch CI
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-chroot\fR
Build stage: force\-refresh the pbuilder chroot first
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-refresh\-chroot\fR
Build stage: never auto\-refresh the pbuilder chroot
.TP
\fB\-\-urgency\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR [default: medium]
Changelog urgency (default medium; e.g. high for security)
.SH UPLOAD
.TP
\fB\-\-upload\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR
Upload stage: dput target (default: dput\*(Aqs own; e.g. mentors)
.TP
\fB\-\-debusine\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Upload stage: publish to a Debusine personal repository instead of a
dput archive. NAME is the repository owner (the r\-NAME\-* workspace
prefix on debusine.debian.net); dbranch uploads with
  dput \-O debusine_workspace=r\-NAME\-<srcpkg>
       \-O debusine_workflow=publish\-to\-sid\-<srcpkg>
(\-\-debusine\-project replaces <srcpkg> for shared workspaces; the
Debian branch targets unstable, whose Debusine suite is sid).
Needs debusine\-client and a `debusine setup` token.
See wiki.debian.org/DebusineDebianNet#Repositories.
.TP
\fB\-\-debusine\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
Upload stage: the Debusine project name — the part after the owner
in the r\-NAME\-PROJECT workspace and publish\-to\-sid\-PROJECT
workflow. Defaults to the source package name, which fits a repo
shipping one package; a shared workspace hosting several packages
names its project here. Requires \-\-debusine.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the commands without running anything (a tutorial)
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Run, but narrate each step + command first (follow along)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress tool output, showing it only when a step fails
.SS dbranch watch-ci
\fBdbranch watch\-ci\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIBRANCH\fR] 
.PP
Watch a branch\*(Aqs GitLab CI pipeline via glab
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR [default: .]
Run in this package working directory
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the commands without running anything (a tutorial)
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
Run, but narrate each step + command first (follow along)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIBRANCH\fR]
Branch to watch (defaults to the current branch)
